    {
      "id": "a4a547d4-7c3a-4703-9ada-6f14e93ab62f",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 860,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## 🧾 What this does\nA complete accounts-payable pipeline: capture invoice emails, extract and categorize them with OpenAI, log to Google Sheets, forecast cash flow, send prioritized alerts, and email a weekly digest.\n\n## ⚙️ How it works\n1. Gmail trigger + PDF text extraction.\n2. OpenAI extracts fields and an expense category; High-value invoices are flagged.\n3. Logged to Google Sheets; month-to-date spend and upcoming payments are calculated.\n4. High-value invoices trigger an approval alert; others a standard notice.\n5. A weekly schedule emails an AP digest.\n\n## 🚀 Setup steps\n1. Connect Gmail, OpenAI, and Google Sheets credentials.\n2. In both Google Sheets nodes, pick your spreadsheet + tab. Header row: vendor, invoice_number, invoice_date, due_date, currency, total_amount, tax_amount, category, priority, summary, email_from, received_at.\n3. In the three email nodes, set your finance/AP team address.\n4. Adjust the High-value threshold in 'Prepare & Prioritize' (default 1000).\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n## 🛠️ Customize\nEdit the category list or fields in the AI node, change the schedule, or tweak the alert thresholds and messages."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
